{
  "assessment_scope": "workflow-final-verification; governed-final; VP1-final-readiness, under rigorloop-records-v3. Assesses the single selected change, all104 changed engineering paths and complete repository/package test population against the current approved proposal, exact one-member Validation Design and one-member Delivery plan. The153 subjects include the fresh149-subject engineering/contract/caller package and four relied-on approval records. The normalized verification_basis binds the GitHub repository ID, SSH push remote, branches and immutable revisions; it is the external handoff basis, not a release authorization.",
  "change_id": "2026-09-16-test-design-and-suite-organization",
  "changes": [
    "Refine the living Validation Design with TEST-SR-19/20, VAL-SR-32, VAL-DEC-11, scenario/helper responsibilities and worked examples; link contributor guidance to the owned rules.",
    "Organize mixed Skill, Validation, Packaging and Release tests into cohesive native groups with ordinary fixture composition. Retain useful existing Node and small validator boundaries, expand compressed scenarios and preserve supported collection/entrypoints.",
    "Make tested actions and independent expected outcomes visible; correct demonstrated omission, rerun, interaction, logging, containment, cleanup, concurrent-writer and rotation-oracle weaknesses with attributable negative proof.",
    "Reconcile source mappings and exact adapter selector identities. Preserve every original test and meaningful variant, expose one existing packed sequence as its own case and account for the complete final35-entrypoint/1373-case population."
  ],
